## 4. Direct data points for strategist use

Use verbatim in the Stage 2 synthesis:

1. **On program scale:** "MWAA's joint capital program moved from $9.0 billion in January 2025 to $20–22.5 billion in July 2026 — a roughly 2.4x expansion in eighteen months, concentrated at IAD." (Sources: WUSA9 and Aerotime.)
2. **On CPE trajectory:** "IAD's 2025 signatory-airline cost per enplanement is $11.17, the lowest since 2005; Moody's expects MWAA's adjusted debt per O&D enplanement to rise from $223 in 2024 to roughly $400 by 2028, and net-revenue DSCR to fall from 1.63x to about 1.3x." (Sources: FFXnow and Bond Buyer.)
3. **On the cost-of-change asymmetry:** "The MacLeamy curve treats early-design changes as keystrokes and late changes as change orders. Commercial acoustic-mitigation guidance puts post-construction sound-absorption retrofits at 30–50% above integrated design and structural sound-isolation retrofits at multiples of the original cost." (Sources: Daniel Davis on MacLeamy; Commercial Acoustics.)
4. **On the overrun record:** "Berlin Brandenburg opened nine years late at €6.5–7.3 billion against a €2.83 billion baseline; the LAX Automated People Mover is $880 million over its $1.9 billion baseline and roughly three years late; Denver's baggage system ran approximately $560 million over budget. Heathrow T5, delivered on time and on £4.3 billion budget under an integrated performance-specification agreement, is the exception that proves the rule." (Sources: budgetoverrun.com; LAist; Ketan Keshav / Medium citing GAO; Mott MacDonald.)
5. **On the technical baseline for a MWAA standard:** "ACRP Research Report 175 recommends a signal-to-noise ratio of ≥10 dB(A) and STI ≥0.45 for pier-style departure lounges; NFPA 72 sets STI ≥0.50 for emergency voice-alarm systems in required areas. A MWAA quiet-by-design standard is not exotic — it is the codification of what airport engineers already treat as good practice, priced pre-award rather than post-commissioning." (Sources: ACRP Report 175; NFPA 72 via context packet.)

